cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. Please also cite the
  third-party datasets, simulators and algorithms listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
title: "RoboForge: Learning Robotic Manipulation Through Diffusion"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Holt
    given-names: Zackary
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-3965-4043"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-09"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/zackholt05-tech/roboforge"
abstract: >-
  A controlled empirical comparison of deterministic behavior cloning, recurrent behavior
  cloning and a conditional diffusion action policy on simulated 3D robotic manipulation
  (robosuite Lift and Can in MuJoCo, robomimic proficient-human demonstrations), evaluated by
  closed-loop rollouts from paired held-out initial states under protocols frozen before the
  test. Includes a separately frozen RGB study and a DP3-inspired point-cloud study, an
  interactive 3D site built from recorded episodes, and a technical report (a local build, not
  peer reviewed) whose numbers are generated from the frozen result files. Simulation only.
keywords:
  - imitation learning
  - diffusion policy
  - behavior cloning
  - robot manipulation
  - robosuite
  - MuJoCo
